WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.801
A one-minute walkthrough of BudgetFlow, recorded in the running app.

2
00:00:02.801 --> 00:00:05.103
A brand-new demo account. Every figure that follows comes from what we enter.

3
00:00:05.103 --> 00:00:12.392
Add an account with its starting balance.

4
00:00:12.392 --> 00:00:23.335
Record October income: a $3,200 salary.

5
00:00:23.335 --> 00:00:33.421
Add an expense: $1,400 rent.

6
00:00:33.421 --> 00:00:43.413
Three more expenses: groceries, transport and dining (shown at 2× speed).

7
00:00:43.413 --> 00:00:45.616
All five entries appear in Transactions.

8
00:00:45.616 --> 00:00:48.767
After a full page reload, the entries are still there: they’re saved in the database.

9
00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:56.410
Set an $80 monthly budget for dining out.

10
00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.998
$72.80 of $80 is spent, so the budget warns before the limit is reached.

11
00:00:58.998 --> 00:01:05.712
Back on the dashboard: totals, charts and budget progress reflect the entries.

12
00:01:05.712 --> 00:01:08.914
The finished dashboard, built entirely from the entries above.
